Query:
--Description:  The original query returned no rows because no snapshots have a refresh_date between
--              1-Sep-2024 and 14-Sep-2024.  The data we need is identified by the “week” values
--              (2024-09-01 and 2024-09-08) but was refreshed later (early October).  
--              Fix-up steps:  
--              1) Filter on “week” instead of “refresh_date” to capture those two weeks.  
--              2) Keep the weekday restriction on refresh_date (Monday-Friday → DAYOFWEEK 1-5) so
--                 we still see weekday snapshots only.  
--              3) Limit to ranks 1-3 and sort newest-to-oldest by refresh_date, then by rank.
SELECT
    "refresh_date",
    "week",
    "rank",
    "term"
FROM GOOGLE_TRENDS.GOOGLE_TRENDS.TOP_TERMS
WHERE "week" BETWEEN '2024-09-01' AND '2024-09-14'
  AND DAYOFWEEK("refresh_date") BETWEEN 1 AND 5   -- Monday-Friday snapshots
  AND "rank" IN (1, 2, 3)
ORDER BY "refresh_date" DESC, "rank"
LIMIT 20
